<http://data.silknow.org/object/9df87378-37c2-34b0-b7b8-71d0a9c549cc>
        a                   ecrm:E73_Information_Object ;
        rdfs:comment        "Densely patterned in a palette of blue, red, green, and yellow, this hanging is one of the earliest Ottoman embroideries in the RISD Museum collection. It features several typically Turkish design elements: vertical serpentine bands with scale-like designs, artichoke palmettes, and the çintamani motif of three balls or crescents. This panel has been patched in several places, probably with pieces taken from its missing lower border." , "Ottoman Turkish Interior Textiles from the Aldrich Collection" , "January 22 - July 17, 2016" ;
        ecrm:P129_is_about  <http://data.silknow.org/object/611e5f49-50c9-3d46-8e86-141463edbfe8> ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    "Exhibition" ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Densely patterned in a palette of blue, red, green, and yellow, this hanging is one of the earliest Ottoman embroideries in the RISD Museum collection. It features several typically Turkish design elements: vertical serpentine bands with scale-like designs, artichoke palmettes, and the çintamani motif of three balls or crescents. This panel has been patched in several places, probably with pieces taken from its missing lower border." , "Ottoman Turkish Interior Textiles from the Aldrich Collection" , "January 22 - July 17, 2016" ;
        schema:contentUrl   <https://risdmuseum.org/exhibitions-events/exhibitions/ottoman-turkish-interior-textiles-aldrich-collection> .

